This file documents the third-party components that are statically linked into the
two upstream binaries shipped by this package (airupnp and aircast, for aarch64 and
x86_64). It is the machine-readable companion to docs/LICENSES.zh-CN.md (S5 audit).

The package author's own wrapper code remains under the repository root MIT license.
The binaries themselves are prebuilt by upstream philippe44/AirConnect and embed the
licenses listed below. This is NOT a blanket "MIT" declaration.

================================================================================
1. INVENTORY — what is actually linked into the shipped ELF binaries
================================================================================

Evidence method (reproducible):
  - Dependency set is taken from the pinned submodule SHAs at git tag 1.12.4
    (.gitmodules + `git ls-tree -r 1.12.4 | awk '$1=="160000"').
  - Actual linkage is proven by a relocation-insensitive byte-run match:
    each .o's .text/.rodata relocation-free runs (>=24 bytes) must appear
    verbatim in the statically linked ELF. Negative control against an unrelated
    binary returns ~0; the known-linked SHINE library returns 98/98.
  - Both binaries are confirmed fully static (`readelf -d` shows no dynamic section).

